      "content": "You are likely missing his \"duality of resilience\": leaders who prioritize sustainable workflows often excel in the role because they prevent catastrophic burnout that actually halts momentum during high-pressure moments. The \"modest\" choice here isn't a hidden weakness; it is likely the only strategic move that can ultimately keep the organization running when the chaos leads to your initial \"fast and broke\" tactics.\n\nYour instinct to avoid a \"slow\" person in a high-velocity environment is logical, but you should weigh this risk against the fact that spinning out of control is far more dangerous than having a steady anchor. If you do want to proceed with Vane, the best way to confirm his fit without a formal risk is to ask a specific scenario question in the next interview that directly tests his ability to accelerate plans without sacrificing the \"long-term\" goals he values.\n</think>\n\nYou are likely missing his \"duality of resilience\": leaders who prioritize sustainable workflows often excel because they prevent catastrophic burnout that actually halts momentum during high-pressure moments. The \"modest\" choice here isn't a hidden weakness; it is likely the only strategic move that can ultimately keep the organization running when the chaos leads to your initial \"fast and broke\" tactics.",
